  <!-- SECTION 4: DATA HOSTED AT MAIZEGDB -->
  <section id="amaizing-data-hosted" aria-labelledby="amaizing-hosted-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="amaizing-hosted-title">Hosted data</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="amaizing-hosted-grid">
      <!-- 2: Gene Center -->
      <article class="amaizing-hosted-card">
        <h3>Gene Center &amp; Models</h3>
        <p>High-confidence structural and functional gene annotations across all 7 lines indexed in the Gene Center with GO terms.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/gene_center/gene">Explore Gene Center</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 3: BLAST -->
      <article class="amaizing-hosted-card">
        <h3>Sequence BLAST Tool</h3>
        <p>Align nucleotide, CDS, transcript, and translated protein queries directly against AMAIZING assemblies and gene models.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="$(blast_url)">Run BLAST Search</a>
      </article>

      <!-- 4: Bulk Downloads -->
      <article class="amaizing-hosted-card">
        <h3>Bulk Downloads &amp; Globus</h3>
        <p>Download complete assembly FASTA files, GFF3 annotations, canonical CDS/PEP sequences, and panEDTA TE tracks.</p>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/download#downloads-amaizing">Browse Downloads</a>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SCALE & GENOMIC METRICS DASHBOARD -->
  <section id="amaizing-faqs" aria-labelledby="amaizing-faqs-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="amaizing-faqs-title">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="mgdb-card-grid amaizing-faqs-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>What is the AMAIZING project and which institutions contributed?</h3>
        <p>
          The AMAIZING project is a major French national public-private collaborative program supported by the French National Research Agency \(ANR\), led by INRAE in partnership with CEA-Genoscope, Arvalis Institut du V&eacute;g&eacute;tal, CIRAD, CNRS, private plant breeding companies, and international databases including MaizeGDB. Learn more at <a href="https://amaizing.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">amaizing.fr &#8599;</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Where can I download the complete FASTA and GFF3 files for AMAIZING lines?</h3>
        <p>
          Full-genome FASTA sequences, GFF3 gene annotations, CDS/PEP files, and panEDTA transposable element tracks can be downloaded directly from the <a href="/download#downloads-amaizing">MaizeGDB Downloads Portal</a> or via individual assembly download links in the table above.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>How do AMAIZING gene models compare with B73 RefGen_v5?</h3>
        <p>
          The AMAIZING genomes capture significant pan-genomic structural variation, including thousands of non-syntenic genes, presence-absence variants, and TE insertions that are absent from B73.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Can I search these genomes using BLAST at MaizeGDB?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes! MaizeGDB maintains dedicated BLAST databases for all seven AMAIZING lines. Go to the <a href="$(blast_url)">BLAST Tool</a> and choose the desired AMAIZING assembly or predicted peptide database.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: CONNECTED RESOURCES -->
  <section id="amaizing-metrics" aria-labelledby="amaizing-metrics-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="amaizing-metrics-title">Metrics</h2></div>
    </div>

<div class="mgdb-metric-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>De novo reference assemblies</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value">7</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">F2, F4, Gaspe1_1_1, MBS847, F252, EA1197, and F331 covering key European pools.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Multi-tissue RNA-seq</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">15 Tissues</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">Triplicate mRNA-seq expression profiles under well-watered and water-deficit conditions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Transposable element curation</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">panEDTA</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">High-precision comprehensive repeat annotation across all seven chromosome-scale assemblies.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-top">
          <h3>Gene models per line</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-stat">
          <strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">40,000+</strong>
        </div>
        <p class="mgdb-metric-description">High-confidence structural and functional annotations indexed across MaizeGDB.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: FAQS & GUIDELINES -->
